Here is an iterative version:

```rust
fn binary_search(xs: &[i32], target: i32) -> Option<usize> {
    let (mut lo, mut hi) = (0usize, xs.len());
    while lo < hi {
        let mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;
        match xs[mid].cmp(&target) {
            std::cmp::Ordering::Less => lo = mid + 1,
            std::cmp::Ordering::Greater => hi = mid,
            std::cmp::Ordering::Equal => return Some(mid),
        }
    }
    None
}
```

The invariant is that if `target` is present, its index lies in the half-open range `lo..hi`. Every iteration shrinks that range while keeping the invariant true, so when the range becomes empty we know the value is absent. Computing `mid` as `lo + (hi - lo) / 2` avoids overflow.

